  "description": "Kaziranga National Park is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of India's finest wildlife destinations. Famous for the world's largest population of the Indian One-Horned Rhinoceros, the park is also home to Royal Bengal Tigers, Asian Elephants, Wild Water Buffaloes, Swamp Deer, and over 450 species of birds. Its grasslands, wetlands, and forests make it a paradise for wildlife lovers and photographers.",

